[
{ type: install }
pqfreebsd is staged, not enforcing.

This package is meant to be operated by a sufficiently advanced LLM that
can follow the skills in %%DATADIR%%/skills/SKILL.md: interview, test*
before one*, Known issues, pqac(7) PRAXIS, T14 (claims degrade by conjunct),
T16 (parameterized bounds). The port cannot measure "sufficiently advanced."

    pqfreebsd-llm-check
    sysrc pqfreebsd_llm_attested=YES   # only if the check matches the model you have
    service pqfreebsd teststage        # then onesnapshot / onestage / ...

oneenforce is refused while pqfreebsd_llm_attested is not YES on a
via-port install. That is the install conjunct, not A_M. A missing LLM
does not un-prove write-up on a box that was already labeled.

oneboot (splash, Forth logo) still requires BOOT_SATISFIED=YES.
TPM is not this pass. Do not kldload mac_lomac until a test window.

Sibling: freebsd-mac-grok (not vendored). Pin a commit.
{ type: remove }
Uninstall restores PREINSTALL *behavior* if you ran oneuninstall.
ZFS snapshots are not destroyed. pkg remove is not zfs rollback.
]
